<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andries Pretorius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1853</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andries Pretorius was a Voortrekker leader who commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> force that defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a> at Blood River in December 1838, securing the Natalia Republic. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed Natal he moved inland, led resistance to British rule north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> and was defeated at Boomplaats in 1848. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sand-river-convention">Sand River Convention</a> of 1852 recognised the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> Boers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> was named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius.jpg" alt="Andries Pretorius" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andries_Pretorius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
